<title>USA: Fidelity Bancorp adopts rights plan.</title>
<headline>Fidelity Bancorp adopts rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Bancorp Inc on Tuesday said its board approved a rights plan with a 15 percent trigger to protect its shareholders against abusive or coercive takeover bids.</p>
<p>One right would be distributed for each share of the company's common stock held as of the March 3 record date, the company said.</p>
<p>In general, rights could not be exercised unless and until 15 percent or more of the company's common stock was acquired by a group, individual or entity, it said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
